From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Build Fix <build@local>
Date: Mon, 23 Jun 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] python3: fix missing X509_VERIFY_PARAM_get_hostflags

OpenSSL < 1.1.1l (including 1.1.1f used in OpenWrt) does not define
X509_VERIFY_PARAM_get_hostflags, causing the _ssl module to fail to
import at runtime with an "undefined symbol" error.

Provide a macro stub that returns 0 when the function is not available.
This is safe because the return value (flags) is only used for
informational purposes and 0 is the default.

---
 feeds/packages/lang/python/python3/patches/028-fix-openssl-missing-hostflags.patch | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 feeds/packages/lang/python/python3/patches/028-fix-openssl-missing-hostflags.patch

diff --git a/feeds/packages/lang/python/python3/patches/028-fix-openssl-missing-hostflags.patch b/feeds/packages/lang/python/python3/patches/028-fix-openssl-missing-hostflags.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1234567
--- /dev/null
+++ b/feeds/packages/lang/python/python3/patches/028-fix-openssl-missing-hostflags.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+--- a/Modules/_ssl.c
++++ b/Modules/_ssl.c
+@@ -77,6 +77,10 @@
+ #ifdef LIBRESSL_VERSION_NUMBER
+ /* LibreSSL does not define this for some reason, but it does implement it */
+ unsigned int X509_VERIFY_PARAM_get_hostflags(X509_VERIFY_PARAM *param);
+ #endif
++#ifndef X509_VERIFY_PARAM_get_hostflags
++/* OpenSSL < 1.1.1l: no-op stub */
++#define X509_VERIFY_PARAM_get_hostflags(param) (0)
++#endif
+ 
+ struct py_ssl_error_code {
+     const char *mnemonic;
